:"Oui, un papier de chanvre grossier, utilisé pour emballer","en":"Yes, a coarse hemp paper used for wrapping"},{"fr":"Non, rien du tout","en":"No, nothing at all"},{"fr":"Oui, aussi bon que le sien","en":"Yes, as good as his"},{"fr":"Oui, en Europe","en":"Yes, in Europe"}],"answer":0,"why":{"fr":"« yǐjīng yǒu rén zuò guò yì zhǒng hěn cū de zhǐ, shì yòng má zuò de ».","en":"“yǐjīng yǒu rén zuò guò yì zhǒng hěn cū de zhǐ, shì yòng má zuò de”."}},{"q":{"fr":"Qu'observe-t-il au bord de la rivière ?","en":"What does he observe by the river?"},"options":[{"fr":"Une fine couche de fibres de soie qui reste sur les nattes","en":"A thin layer of silk fibre left on the mats"},{"fr":"Des poissons","en":"Fish"},{"fr":"Des enfants qui écrivent dans le sable","en":"Children writing in the sand"},{"fr":"Des feuilles qui flottent","en":"Floating leaves"}],"answer":0,"why":{"fr":"« zhú xí shàng liúxià le yì céng báobáo de sī xiānwéi ».","en":"“zhú xí shàng liúxià le yì céng báobáo de sī xiānwéi”."}},{"q":{"fr":"Quelles matières utilise-t-il ?","en":"What materials does he use?"},"options":[{"fr":"Écorce, vieux tissus, vieux filets de pêche","en":"Bark, old cloth, old fishing nets"},{"fr":"De la soie","en":"Silk"},{"fr":"Du bambou neuf","en":"New bamboo"},{"fr":"Du papier acheté","en":"Bought paper"}],"answer":0,"why":{"fr":"« shùpí, pò mábù, jiù yúwǎng, háiyǒu má tóu ».","en":"“shùpí, pò mábù, jiù yúwǎng, háiyǒu má tóu”."}},{"q":{"fr":"Que dit-il à ses artisans découragés ?","en":"What does he tell his discouraged craftsmen?"},"options":[{"fr":"Chaque échec nous apprend une mauvaise méthode","en":"Each failure teaches us one wrong method"},{"fr":"D'arrêter","en":"To stop"},{"fr":"Qu'ils seront punis","en":"That they will be punished"},{"fr":"Qu'il n'y croit plus","en":"That he no longer believes in it"}],"answer":0,"why":{"fr":"« Měi shībài yí cì, wǒmen jiù zhīdào yì zhǒng bú duì de fāngfǎ. »","en":"“Měi shībài yí cì, wǒmen jiù zhīdào yì zhǒng bú duì de fāngfǎ.”"}},{"q":{"fr":"Avec quoi « pêche »-t-on la pâte à papier ?","en":"What is used to lift the pulp out of the water?"},"options":[{"fr":"Un fin écran en bambou","en":"A fine bamboo screen"},{"fr":"Un filet","en":"A net"},{"fr":"Les mains","en":"The hands"},{"fr":"Une pierre","en":"A stone"}],"answer":0,"why":{"fr":"« Yòng yí gè xì zhú liánzi zài shuǐ lǐ yì lāo ».","en":"“Yòng yí gè xì zhú liánzi zài shuǐ lǐ yì lāo”."}},{"q":{"fr":"Pourquoi appelle-t-on ce papier « Cài hóu zhǐ » ?","en":"Why is the paper called “Cài hóu zhǐ”?"},"options":[{"fr":"Cai Lun a reçu le titre de marquis (hou)","en":"Cai Lun was made a marquis (hou)"},{"fr":"C'est le nom de sa ville","en":"It is his town's name"},{"fr":"C'est le nom de l'impératrice","en":"It is the empress's name"},{"fr":"Parce qu'il est vert","en":"Because it is green"}],"answer":0,"why":{"fr":"Il est fait « Lóngtíng hóu », d'où « Cài hóu zhǐ ».","en":"He was made “Lóngtíng hóu”, hence “Cài hóu zhǐ”."}},{"q":{"fr":"Comment le papier arrive-t-il dans le monde arabe ?","en":"How does paper reach the Arab world?"},"options":[{"fr":"Des artisans chinois capturés à Talas en 751","en":"Chinese craftsmen captured at Talas in 751"},{"fr":"Par un mariage","en":"Through a marriage"},{"fr":"Cai Lun y est allé","en":"Cai Lun went there"},{"fr":"Par la mer","en":"By sea"}],"answer":0,"why":{"fr":"Ils sont emmenés à Samarcande, qui devient une ville du papier.","en":"They are taken to Samarkand, which becomes a paper city."}},{"q":{"fr":"Quelles sont les « quatre grandes inventions » ?","en":"What are the “Four Great Inventions”?"},"options":[{"fr":"Le papier, la boussole, la poudre et l'imprimerie","en":"Paper, the compass, gunpowder and printing"},{"fr":"Le papier, la soie, le thé et la porcelaine","en":"Paper, silk, tea and porcelain"},{"fr":"La Grande Muraille, le canal, le papier et la boussole","en":"The Great Wall, the canal, paper and the compass"},{"fr":"L'écriture, les chiffres, la roue et le feu","en":"Writing, numbers, the wheel and fire"}],"answer":0,"why":{"fr":"« zàozhǐshù hé zhǐnánzhēn, huǒyào, yìnshuāshù ».","en":"“zàozhǐshù hé zhǐnánzhēn, huǒyào, yìnshuāshù”."}}],"id":"cailun","order":105,"category":"history","level":"hsk3","hanzi":"蔡伦造纸","titlePinyin":"Cài Lún zào zhǐ","title":{"fr":"Cai Lun et l'invention du papier","en":"Cai Lun and the Invention of Paper"},"era":{"fr":"vers 63 – 121 apr. J.-C.","en":"c. AD 63 – 121"},"summary":{"fr":"Une impératrice lit des montagnes de lamelles de bambou ; la soie coûte une fortune. Un serviteur du palais observe les femmes qui lavent le coton au bord de la rivière… et fabrique ce que le monde entier utilise encore.","en":"An empress reads mountains of bamboo slips; silk costs a fortune. A palace servant watches women washing cotton by the river… and makes something the whole world still uses."},"chars":1822}